'''Yerba Buena''' ([[Baliscano language|Baliscano]] for "{{W|Yerba buena|good herb}}"; {{Langx|gug|Ka'agatu}}, {{Literal translation|place of the pleasant herb}}) is a commune in the [[Luzamontaña]] region of [[Araucaria]]. Located on the [[Guadalquivir]], it is an [[Aethiopian Ocean|Aethiopic]] port city, and the gateway to the [[Castejón|Baliscan capital]]. In April 2025, it was determined that Yerba Buena had a population of 1,036,563, making it the third-most populous city in the [[Alpujarra]], the fifth-most populous in the Araucarian community, and the [[List of largest Baliscan cities by population|eleventh-most-populous]] in Balisca overall. It is considered as a [[w:satellite city|satellite community]] of the [[Castejón Metropolis]].

The city's name references a number of aromatic plants grown in the area, most of which belong to the {{W|mint family}}. The specific plant species regarded as the namesake is unknown, varying dependent on what species are customarily grown in {{W|Community gardening|communal}} {{W|communal garden|garden}}s. Since [[Araucaria]]'s legalization of recreational cannabis use in 1878, the term has been increasingly associated with the cultivation of {{W|marijuana}} and {{W|hemp}}, both of which the city produces in large numbers. Yerba Buena has since developed an influential {{W|cannabis culture}}, and the city declared {{W|420 (cannabis culture)|4/20}} to be a [[Public holidays in Balisca|public holiday]] in 1975, becoming the first Baliscan polity to do so. It is where the [[Cosmopolitan Church of Cannabis]], a confederaly-recognized {{W|new religious movement}} which uses cannabis as a sacrament, was founded in 2001.

Yerba Buena's territory covers what was once a mosaic of [[w:California coastal prairie|coastal terrace prairie]], [[W:Vachellia caven|''churque'']] and [[W:Aspidosperma quebracho-blanco|''kebrako'']] {{W|woodland}}, and {{W|coastal scrub}} or {{W|tussock grass}}lands. Following the [[Baliscan Civil War]], the territory was recognized by the [[Anyos Federales|Baliscan government]] as "[[Maroon Confederacy|Maroon]]" inline with the [[Kafto-Ethiopian Charter]].

The fertile flatland soils helped it become a prolific agricultural region. In the late 1860s, Yerba Buena became the western terminal of the [[Alpujarra Railway]]. Following the [[1924 Alpujarra earthquake]], many citizens of surrounding areas moved to Yerba Buena, enlarging the population, increasing its housing stock, and improving its infrastructure.
